cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "STRATUM: how well can persistent contrails be predicted over India?"
message: "If you use this software or its derived data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Shrugal
    family-names: Vinod
  - given-names: Aditya
    family-names: Harsoda
  - given-names: Ishaan
    family-names: Kupnur
  - given-names: Abeer
    family-names: Shah
contact:
  - name: "STRATUM team, Indus International School, Bengaluru"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered study of persistent aircraft contrails over India (6–37°N, 68–98°E): ERA5-based
  contrail physics checked against contrails detected by Meteosat-9, a learned correction, and a
  conservative ranking of altitude changes by the lower bound of net warming avoided.
  Computational estimates only; air traffic control feasibility is not modelled.
keywords:
  - contrails
  - aviation climate impact
  - ERA5
  - Meteosat
  - India
  - pre-registration
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ShrugalVinod/stratum"
url: "https://stratum.aerospaceonyx.workers.dev"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
